Key Takeaways
Merge preserves branch history and is safe for shared branches.
Rebase creates a cleaner, linear history by replaying commits.
Interactive rebase lets you reorder, edit, or squash commits.
Avoid rebasing branches that others are actively using.
Follow your team's branching and merge policy rather than using one approach everywhere.